<title>USA: Fed adds reserves via $2.0 billion customer RPs.</title>
<headline>Fed adds reserves via $2.0 billion customer RPs.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve added temporary reserves to the banking system on Friday through $2.0 billion customer repurchase agreements, a Fed spokeswoman confirmed.</p>
<p>Analysts had expected the Fed to either refrain from open market operations because of the soft Federal funds rate or to add temporary reserves to the banking system through term system repurchase agreements.</p>
</text>
